When `--dir` is set, the install no longer asks for an agent and no longer needs a scope, because `resolveInstallDir` already returns `opts.Dir` in that case. I changed `resolveHosts` so that with `--dir` and no `--agent` it returns a single placeholder host. `buildInstallPlans` then groups by directory, so one plan is built for that directory. Once the user chooses the destination, the placeholder is only used for display (`formatPlanHosts`) and for telemetry (`mapAgentHostsToIDs`). The Kiro hint only fires for an explicit `kiro-cli` agent.

I picked `registry.DefaultAgentID` for the placeholder, which means the telemetry `agent_hosts` value reports `github-copilot` for `--dir` installs. The alternative is a synthetic host with ID `custom`, which would be more honest in telemetry. I went with the default to keep the change minimal.

